{title: Four Hundred Shekels}
{subtitle: Genesis 23:1–10; 23:10–11; 23:12–13; 23:14–16; 23:17–20; 49:29–32}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 74}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Gm7] | [Eb] |
| [F] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Sarah died in Hebron land
A [Gm7]hundred twen-ty-sev-en years she stayed [Eb]
[Bb]Abrose up to speak the word
A [Gm7]stranger in the foreign [Fsus4]world [F]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I am a [Eb]sojourner among you
Give me a burial [Bb]site to view
[Bbmaj7/A]The [Gm7]Hittites spoke with gentle voice
[Eb]You are a prince before God's [F]choice
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Ephron sat in the city gate [Bb]
Said I give you field [Bbmaj7/A]and [Gm7]cave
No, my lord, hear [Gm7/F]me [Eb]please
I will pay the price with [Fsus4]ease [F]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb]Abraham bowed before the crowd
And [Gm7]told them all what they should [Eb]
[Bb]Plead with Ephron son of Zohar
[Gm7]To sell the cave and open [Fsus4]door
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Ephron sat in the city gate [Bb]
Said I give you field [F/A]and [Gm7]cave
No, my lord, hear me [Gm7/F][Eb]please
I will pay the price with [Fsus4]ease
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]Four hundred shekels silver weighed
[Bb/D]In the hearing of the peo[Gm7]ple
[Eb]Abraham agreed to terms
And bought the land with his arms
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Fsus4]The [Bb]field of Machpelah passed
[Gm7]Into the hand of the fa[Eb]ther
[Bb]All trees within the border
[Gm7]Now belong to him forev[Fsus4]er
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Ephron sat in the city gate [Bb]
Said I give you field [Bbmaj7/A]and [Gm7]cave
No, my lord, hear me [Gm7/F][Eb]please
I will pay the price with [Fsus4]ease
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Buried Sarah in the [Eb]cave
[Fsus4]In the land of Ca[Bb]naan
{end_of_verse}

